{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960682,"nonce":"TQ+OE/8iUtvdBH51Rum8aKcZjcQ=","title":"gpu/build.rs empties the hand-written Haxe files it copies","message":"`write_haxe(\u0026PathBuf::from(\"haxe\"))` copies every committed file in `haxe/rayzor/gpu` into `haxe/rayzor/gpu`. The guard `entry.path() != destination` compares an absolute source path with a relative destination, so it never holds, and `std::fs::copy` of a file onto itself truncates it.\n\nSince 80dbaec0 (which made the call unconditional) six files are committed at 0 bytes: GPUCompute.hx (8953 bytes at 80dbaec0~1), Mat4.hx (2127), ShaderMath.hx (2010), Vec2.hx (739), Vec3.hx (1011), Vec4.hx (994). Every build empties them again.","files":null}]}